To solve this problem, we will start by combining the numbers 14 and 4 using addition. Then, we will use the result to work with 3 and 3 using subtraction.

Step 1: 14 + 4 = 18 \quad \text{(addition)}
Step 2: 18 - 3 = 15 \quad \text{(subtraction)}
Step 3: 15 + 3 = 18 \quad \text{(addition) This is the result we need to get to 21!}
Final Expression: 14 + 4 - 3 + 3 = 18

